doc Rename rule: every name a package or truck defines that starts with a prefix.
  ```
  resolve
    rename prefix 'fs_' in filesystem to 'filesys_'
  end
  ```

  Each name the scope defines (functions, globals, constants, structs) that
  starts with `fs_` gets the new prefix instead: `fs_list` becomes
  `filesys_list`. References are renamed in the scope and in every package
  that needs it; see [resolve](../resolve.md). It is an error if the scope
  defines no such name.
